    excerpt: "This workflow turns a Google Sheet of leads into automated, personalized cold outreach. A Google Sheets trigger polls every minute for new rows. An If node filters out any row already flagged in the done column so leads are processed only once. The workflow then sets your company details (name, activity, sender email) and begins enrichment. It calls the twitter-api47 RapidAPI endpoint to resolve the lead's handle into a user ID, pulls their recent tweets, and a Code node trims the result to the 10 latest posts. It then calls the Fresh LinkedIn Profile Data RapidAPI endpoint using the lead's linkedin_url and trims their LinkedIn activity to 10 posts as well. Both post sets are passed into a GPT-4o chain that is instructed to find a common activity between your company and the prospect, then write an outreach email. A structured output parser forces clean JSON with a subject and an HTML cover_letter. The email is sent over SMTP directly to the lead, with your own address CC'd for tracking. Finally the Google Sheets node updates the row and marks it done so it will not be processed again. The value here is research-backed personalization at volume. Instead of manually reading each prospect's social feeds and writing a custom email, the operator drops leads into a sheet and the workflow handles scraping, angle-finding, drafting, and sending. Free RapidAPI tiers cap usage at roughly 500 tweets and 100 LinkedIn profiles per month, which sets the practical scale. The prompt is fully editable so you can match your tone or plug in a known copy framework.",
